!
! What one form of capital shows as held, in minor units, in Trebago
! (ninefold_model.h NF2): minor for a priceable form, 0 for a
! state-reserved one (4 .. 7). For integers min(1, max(0, form - 3)) *
! min(1, max(0, 8 - form)) is 1 exactly when 4 <= form <= 7. Trebago is
! exact and answers any form and any sum that fits 64 bits, where Sutra
! refuses a form past 8, a negative, or a sum past 18 digits: held.
trebago holding
  in  form(n), minor(n)
  out holding(n)
  holding(i) = minor(i) * (1 - min(1, max(0, form(i) - 3)) * min(1, max(0, 8 - form(i))))
end
